{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/926155-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-retrospective","id":926155,"title":"Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines Retrospective","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-04T16:37:50-07:00","id":926155,"title":"Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines Retrospective","content":"This is a thread for discussing the Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines game. I know we're all hoping for Onyx Path to license a sequel to Obsidian (I hope it's set in Chicago personally or New Orleans) but I wanted to talk to you guys about it. What was your favorite part of the game? Least favorite part?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2014/07/vampire-masquerade-bloodlines-review.html\" target=\"_blank\">For me, it really was one of the best RPGs ever made.</a><br /> <br /> I mean, the last third sucked but that was just by comparison to the original. It's a shame they never did a console release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-04-2016, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T00:44:17-07:00","id":926312,"title":"","content":"Favorite would be the mood and feel. There has been no video game that makes me feel like Bloodlines makes me feel. It's that combination of menacing and sexy. It's moody, it's exciting. It's a night of clubbing, it's standing on the street at 3 am deciding where to go next. I have never played a video game that felt like it, and TT games by other GMs has been rare.<br /> <br /> Honorable mention to NPCs. So.Good. I love the characters in this game. Only a HM because it is far from alone there.<br /> <br /> Least favorite is combat. Terrible. Few games combat I have played in the past 20 years have sucked as hard as Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Dishonorable mention the last...4th or so? The end of Chinatown and the rest are weak. Well, Giovanni mansion is not bad, but other than that. It becomes a killefest, with combat as the low point.<br /> <br /> Still, it is an amazing game. My #3 of all time and only non Bioware in my top 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T09:11:44-07:00","id":926450,"title":"","content":"Obviously, from my avatar(and name), you can tell I'm a huge fan of the game. Easily my favorite game of all time(and Redemption is not far behind it). Almost everything about the game is amazing(except for the combat, which is merely OKAY). <br /> <br /> The real world setting and story, which has yet to be as well accomplished by any game before or since it's release, is top notch. Downtown L.A., Santa Monica, Hollywood(my favorite), and Chinatown are all a blast to play through. The feel of the characters is awesome; many of which are some of the greatest NPC's in the history of gaming. Smiling Jack, Damsel, Nines, LaCroix, Ming Xiao, etc. hold up extremely well, have voice actors who poured themselves into the roles, and are all different from each other.<br /> <br /> The soundtrack is fantastic. God, I could go on and on about this game. When Bloodlines 2 is announced, I'm not entirely sure if I'll be able to contain myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:41:17-07:00","id":926542,"title":"","content":"Yea the soundtrack really bears mention. That and how several of the quests have different outcomes. Not all of them, but there is often more than one way to skin a cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img ite